      ":question/id": "f8867c14-c978-5609-8feb-155bfedae13c",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-70889",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =6e\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =6e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{6e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
